3.1.0
* Add a stacktrace to the records to show where the searches were originated #13
* Fix django-debug-toolbar >= 4.1 compatibility ('_thread._local' object has no attribute 'collection') #21
* Replace pkg_resources with importlib.metadata; works in environments without setuptools #23 #18
* Replace deprecated debug-toolbar get_stack()/tidy_stacktrace() with get_stack_trace() #25
* Fix "Show Json Body" / "Show Json Response" / "Show Stacktrace" toggles, dead with lazily
  loaded panel content in modern debug-toolbar; now native details/summary without JavaScript #28
* Fix "DEBUG is set to False" being shown in the panel even when DEBUG is True #28
* Fix empty records (no hash/time/url/body) with debug-toolbar >= 5: panel stats are now
  JSON-serializable, surviving the toolbar's serialized stats store #31
* Fix apostrophes rendering as literal \u0027 in the JSON body/response display, a leftover
  from embedding JSON into inline JavaScript #34
* Support elasticsearch 8.x and 9.x by hooking elastic_transport instead of the removed
  Connection.log_request_success (#19); elasticsearch 7.x keeps its original hook #37
* Fix memory leak (#7): queries are now collected only between the panel's request start and
  stats generation, instead of accumulating in every thread that once served a toolbar request #32
* Test against currently supported versions: Django up to 6.1, debug-toolbar up to 7.1,
  Python up to 3.14 #26; expand test coverage #27
* Run tests on pull requests, split from PyPI publishing; modernize CI and pre-commit #24 #26

3.0.2
* Just CI auto deploy fixes

